# docs-mcp-server

MCP server with vector search over documents. Everything runs in a single Docker container.

## Features

- **search** — semantic search over documents (top 5 by default)
- **fetch** — retrieve full document by ID

Documents (MD files) are parsed, chunked, and vectorized at image build time. ChromaDB + sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) — all local, no external APIs.

## Build and Run

```bash
# Build (data indexing happens during build)
docker build -t docs-mcp-server .

# Run (HTTPS by default, self-signed cert)
docker run -p 8000:8000 docs-mcp-server

# Connect: https://localhost:8000/mcp
# (ignore certificate warning)
```

## CLI (Local)

```bash
python -m src.cli build --data-dir ./data --chroma-path ./chroma_db
python -m src.cli search "getting started" --top-k 3
python -m src.cli fetch some_doc_id
```

## Tests

```bash
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
pytest -q
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `HOST` | `0.0.0.0` | Host to bind to |
| `PORT` | `8000` | Port |
| `ENABLE_AUTH` | `false` | Enable authentication |
| `API_KEY` | — | API key (when ENABLE_AUTH=true) |
| `SSL_KEYFILE` | `/app/ssl/key.pem` | Path to SSL key |
| `SSL_CERTFILE` | `/app/ssl/cert.pem` | Path to SSL certificate |
| `MISTRAL_BASE_URL` | — | Base URL for Mistral-compatible embeddings API |
| `MISTRAL_API_KEY` | — | API key for embeddings |
| `MISTRAL_EMBEDDINGS_PATH` | `/v1/embeddings` | Embeddings path appended to base URL |
| `MISTRAL_EMBEDDINGS_URL` | — | Full embeddings endpoint (overrides base+path) |
| `MISTRAL_MODEL` | `mistral-embed` | Embedding model name |
| `MISTRAL_BATCH_SIZE` | `32` | Batch size for embedding calls |
| `MISTRAL_TIMEOUT_S` | `60` | HTTP timeout (seconds) |
| `MISTRAL_SSL_VERIFY` | `true` | Verify SSL certificates |
| `EMBEDDING_MODEL` | `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` | Local model name when using sentence-transformers |

## Authentication

When `ENABLE_AUTH=true` and `API_KEY` is set:

- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>` or `X-API-Key: <API_KEY>`

```bash
docker run -p 8000:8000 \
  -e ENABLE_AUTH=true \
  -e API_KEY=secret123 \
  docs-mcp-server
```

## Adding Documents

Place MD files in `data/` and rebuild the image. Supports up to ~100 files.
